;">The agenda</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Some rather gloomy news to start Friday as=
 Andrew Bailey, the governor of the Bank of England, has warned that Britis=
h banks will probably try to pass on the cost of higher taxes to their cust=
omers.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Last month the chancellor, John Healey, an=
nounced plans to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u=
001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAX2I5fp6olyh5yUeClMls_DPeCiAC=
zYNqx5fPuVnMJWhCZQnusgCQrGkQawagA75uQZMLJyYT9fbWLH2NmXzIG4UfIiC3vXBVHz61aln=
3tMHWPjZTZ0QTfwQyCCR9uI2AxWOS_tDFQJJEGzPMkGhW50dTu-JfPV9oBlogobvKc4QKrCn84Y=
z4H1Faft_k9hFjjwlftv4X8T2qOMVrgCmJbxbmXD8prECtbFD5lZbAQa3alNb_BMeBdU4VWOWjm=
FdBKb2dj1vBXJpRGD1sDKnoQAdC6N05URSA6yZMqe_qHvstGcijHBZAvaaOKja9splM/4w3/8fZ=
1lwdSSomGnACZdNP3bw/h34/h001.-COBhNwRp4gQdCiAN2lBIJdK8KyCKt8D8xinO1oUPCI" s=
tyle=3D"color: #0077B6;">double the bank surcharge</a>, which is levied on =
top of corporation tax, to 6% from January. He said the increase =E2=80=93 =
expected to be worth =C2=A31.5bn =E2=80=93 would be =E2=80=9Ctime-limited=
=E2=80=9D, lasting 15 months, in order =E2=80=9Cto pay for <a href=3D"https=
://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7f=
IEMgszcCSneHEAuG0RqCca7fIwka-i3erzpxRn9uXH-Ubi0mrCQnsV1JJrcOMJSG8KAODp9DxC-=
HBgahkiLgb4bcTkucZg3kQTGHgUNFvqXa_Z3jSGP3v6r85IcbUTQYuk38UJUYjkMedDPFq28TT6=
7sMbn6Eatz6XvM8ycKoEyzO4Pf_2jvliG-1G5p4g3G2Af3aR-4SqjIeefsdC15eh4wBFg4MYTAV=
90nj_mv_voOlSlh2HUk168n3OMbSpxvXDGV6BYI_9L9eY/4w3/8fZ1lwdSSomGnACZdNP3bw/h3=
5/h001.ltnGAubVqf8jpz_TnxYMqY1mEJzhYprru0ui2yU2JBI" style=3D"color: #0077B6=
;">immediate support</a> on energy bills=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But Bailey has told <a href=3D"https://abl=
ink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR1fY8mJ5CqyZmjc=
qMTyt9byOKFfyRHbzM6RvVXsEFAgAHX5TOoCd5wxqd-QaxpnddUkd5prKgxIdNq4TY_A5USE91G=
gaDJFH7ZLfzVfID24dEO7H2Wkcm9x_fC0qmLMB1tG8j9nS9diiHNvrznp4yp4_PTEDSKeZqnpKW=
b8LFakhNKZ8X_OMwzjAU04zO__4HwHsy16Nbl0pjZkCqf1s0Wk_MNOWv4flmlai1LNRrxFja5d5=
AysPRJ47emitIfThN-aE1lJIzAfa4zGcoDqhq-TlwILtqxwbyv4vMsk0wkpOnjinNtD2KcmLteN=
MXsp8qQ/4w3/8fZ1lwdSSomGnACZdNP3bw/h36/h001.gt-zkuXxB0KtjprBdnGcHCPe75YSPYR=
FXqlUaqp2qBs" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the Times</a> that he would not be =
surprised if banks attempted to pass on higher levies so they could =E2=80=
=9Cprotect their earnings=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">He said: =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s a market ec=
onomy, so these are decisions banks will have to take. You could understand=
 that they will look to pass it on because they will be targeting a rate of=
 return.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CNow, how successful they will be =
depends on all sorts of things: market conditions, competition within the i=
ndustry and so on. It wouldn=E2=80=99t be surprising to find out that they =
will start by trying to do that.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Several analysts have predicted that banks=
 will try to offset their higher tax bills by charging higher interest rate=
s on loans or offering less generous saving rates.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Bailey=E2=80=99s comments came as the Bank=
=E2=80=99s latest report found that <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.the=
guardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBKRF7ijFPd=
RR7IMeDcPXVRjqS4eXCz9zZKtBheDpBpoQNpRa2JipxuwZ2AMsxMHC0WG-V1syk11xezRIvb2Fo=
